    "preamble": "Binu K.K vs Food Safety Officer on 6 November, 2014 Author: B. Kemal Pasha Bench: B.Kemal Pasha In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present: The Honourable Mr. Justice B.Kemal Pasha Thursday, The 15Th Day Of February 2018 / 26Th Magha, 1939 Crl.MC.No. 8010 of 2017 ----------------------- Cc 2091/2015 of Judicial First Class Magistrate Court, Chavakkad ------- Petitioners/Accused : -------------------- 1 Binu K.K,Aged 30 Years, S/O. Kochumon, Karoth House, P.O. Kannoth, Manakkalkadavu, Venkitangu Village, (Food Business Operator, Kajah Tea Company Pvt. Ltd, P.B. No. 55,14/117-2, Guruvayur Municipality, Muthuvathur, Guruvayur, Thrissur, Pin-680101) 2 A. Abdul Rafeeq,Aged 47 Years, Managing Director, Kajah Tea Company Pvt. Ltd, P.B. No. 55,14/117-2, Guruvayur Municipality, Muthuvathur, Guruvayur, Thrissur,Pin-680101 3 A. Abdul Rawuf,About 51 Years, Director, Kajah Tea Company Pvt. Ltd, P.B. No. 55,14/117-2, Guruvayur Municipality, Muthuvathur,Guruvayur, Thrissur, Pin-680101) 4 A. Abdul Shafeeq,About 53 Years, Director, Kajah Tea Company Pvt. Ltd, P.B. No. 55,14/117-2, Guruvayur Municipality, Muthuvathur,Guruvayur, Thrissur, Pin-680101. 5 A. Abdul Hazeeb,About 53 Years, Director,Kajah Tea Company Pvt. Ltd, P.B. No. 55,14/117-2, Guruvayur Municipality, Muthuvathur,Guruvayur, Thrissur, Pin-680101. Binu K.K vs Food Safety Officer on 6 November, 2014 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/161313242/ 1 6 A. Abdul Zuhin,Aged About 40 Years, Director, Kajah Tea Company Pvt. Ltd, P.B. No. 55,14/117-2, Guruvayur Municipality, Muthuvathur,Guruvayur, Thrissur, Pin-680101. Crl.MC.No. 8010 of 2017 () --------------------------- 7 M/S. Kajah Tea Company Pvt. Ltd., P.B. No. 55, 14/117-2, Guruvayur Municipality, Muthuvathur,Guruvayur, Thrissur, Pin-680101 (Represented By It'S Managing Director A. Abdul Rafeeq). By Advs.Sri.P.Vijaya Bhanu (Sr.) Sri.M.Revikrishnan Smt.Mitha Sudhindran Sri.K.Prajeesh Respondents/Complainant & State: ------------------------------- 1. Food Safety Officer, Chavakkad Circle, Chavakkad-680 506.",
    "facts": "This is a case relating to the limit of iron filling as per order dated 02.11.2017 of the Director (RCD). All States and Union Territories are directed not to launch prosecutions for non-conformance of limit of iron fillings in cases where samples were picked up/tested prior to 19.05.2016. In this case, sample was drawn on 25.10.2014 and prosecution has been launched for non-conformance of iron fillings.",
